bwa-mem2 v2.3, patched for scripts/smem_capture.sh. Two parts:
  1. Homebrew's arm64 patch (bwa-mem2 PR #281, sse2neon), as the Homebrew oracle is built.
  2. An env-guarded dump in bwamem.cpp: BWA2_SMEM_DUMP=<file> writes every read's SMEMs
     (name m n k l s, after all three rounds) right after mem_collect_smem. Off when unset.
Build (arm64 macOS, `brew install sse2neon`):
  git clone --recursive --branch v2.3 https://github.com/bwa-mem2/bwa-mem2 reference/bwa-mem2
  cd reference/bwa-mem2 && git apply ../../scripts/bwa-mem2-smem-dump.patch
  mkdir -p ext/sse2neon && ln -sf "$(brew --prefix sse2neon)/include/sse2neon.h" ext/sse2neon/
  make all arch=-march=armv8-a CC=clang CXX=clang++ CFLAGS="-Iinclude -fPIC -O2 -DSTDC_HEADERS"
Checked: its SAM on work/ (SE and PE) is byte-identical to Homebrew's bwa-mem2 2.3.

